  "instructions": [
    "Preheat the oven to 400 degrees.",
    "Roll out the puff pastry on a floured surface to a large rectangle.",
    "Place the herring fillets in the center of the pastry, leaving a 1 inch border around them.",
    "Drizzle the olive oil, lemon juice, salt, black pepper, and sumac over the herring.",
    "Top the herring with the pitted dates.",
    "Brush the edges of the pastry with a little water.",
    "Fold the pastry over the herring, pressing the edges to seal.",
    "Place the en croute on a baking sheet lined with parchment paper.",
    "Bake for 20 minutes or until the pastry is golden brown.",
    "Serve hot and enjoy."
  ],
